{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk","id":1208904,"title":"Shadow London - Savage Urban Fantasy in the UK","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-19T09:02:06-07:00","id":1208904,"title":"Shadow London - Savage Urban Fantasy in the UK","content":"Since i first discovered Mage:The Ascension 1e I have been fascinated with the system and the lore and have continued to run mage games through M:Aw, all in a supernatural version of London. But I have been less interested in the focus on the larger metaplots and meta background (Atlantis etc) and focused more on Mages vs the things that go bump in the night. Think Dresden Files vs Cthulhu with a large dash of Neverwhere. My version of the game has developed with Mage paths but replacing the orders with faction that are rooted in magical reflections of mundane realities of modern Britain and geared toward ideology and goals in this world rather than remnants of Atlantean factions. <br /> <br /> <b>Major Influences: </b>OWoD Isles of the Mighty, and Dark Ages Britain, and NWoD Shadows of UK, . The whole Cthulhu Britannica line from Cubicle 7 (currently unavailable as pdf\u2019s as they retool the system), the Fireborn RPG from Fantasy Flight Games, Mythic Britain RPG from Design Mechanics, The Mists of Avalon by Marion Zimmer Bradley, and the Warlord Chronicles by Bernard Cornwell for historical versions of Arthurian myth that are based on real dark ages Celtic Britain. Neverwhere by Neil Gaiman (TV and book), the Rivers of London series by Ben Aaronvitch), the Skyscraper Throne series by Tom Pollack, Good Omens by Neil Gaiman and Terry Pratchett, the Courts of the Feyre series by Mike Shevdon, The Rook by Daniel O\u2019Malley, Doctor Who, Torchwood and Sherlock TV shows.<br /> <br /> <b>Major Magical Factions of Great Britain</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Covenant of York (the Covenant)</b> - In 1089 a supernatural darkness fell on the city of York. Soon a local Mage realized that the reason was a diabolist vampire who had sacrificed his fellow vampires in a ritual pact with a dark god. The mages, the fae, and the two-natured of the City joined forces to defeat the vampire and in the wake of their victory they signed the Covenant of York, agreeing to join together again whenever dark forces threatened the city. Over the course of the next few hundred years this covenant was accepted by other supernatural communities in Britain, although by the 15th century the mages were taking on the vast majority of the responsibility. Eventually, the Covenant became an organization of mages dedicated to protecting the mortal realms of Great Britain from harmful supernatural forces with the broad consent of the other major supernatural factions of the British Isles and throughout the former British Empire. While some supernatural factions resent this presumption on the part of Covenant mages, most tolerate it as long as the Covenant respects their boundaries and mostly concerns itself with otherworldly forces and rogue elements within the supernatural world. After all, why should vampires or fae waste their energies hunting down rogue supernaturals from within their ranks when the mages will do it for them!<br /> <br /> <b>The Sovereignty of Albion (the Sovereigns)</b> - One day King Arthur will return to rule all of Britain. In the meantime, the Sovereigns make it their business to ensure that Britain is protected and kept in good order as they continue to search for ways to reestablish King Arthur\u2019s rule. The Sovereigns are the most politically involved of the magical factions working within mundane politics and industry to ensure Britain\u2019s prosperity and security in preparation for Arthur\u2019s return. The recent Brexit vote has created serious splits within this faction as they, like the rest of Britain, argue over what it really means today to ensure Britain\u2019s greatness and what Britain should look like when Arthur returns to rule it. <br /> <br /> <b>The City Sons </b>- The City Sons are connected to the city on a mystical level. They are urban shamans, worshipers of city gods, old and new, protectors of the city and its inhabitants. There are some City Sons in every major city of Britain but London is where they are most concentrated London isn\u2019t just a city. It is THE city. In truth the City Sons are two factions in one, divided as are mundane city dwellers, between those who love the gleaming, up and coming, urbane parts of the city and those who are committed to the gritty urban areas the former ignore or want to gentrify. In recent years there have been debates about the name of this faction with many arguing about whether it is still appropriate to call themselves the City Sons. Some have begun using City Daughters for female members or just using the term City Children for them all.<br /> <br /> <b>The Druid Circle (the Circle)</b> - The Romans believed they had destroyed the druids but they were wrong. As long as there is a Britain there will be druids committed to the old ways and old gods of Britain. While the City Sons protect the cities, the druids protect the country and the wilds tending to the needs of the land and its people. As such there are few members of the Druid Circle in London but London has grown so much over the centuries, expanding to include places that were previously country and small villages in the surrounding areas that some druids have found themselves protecting former countryside that is now part of greater London. <br /> <br /> <b>The Collegium</b> - The Collegium are seekers of magical knowledge, searching Britain and beyond for hidden and lost magic and engaging in research to explore the limits of modern magic. While many other mages see Collegium mages as bookworms and the magical equivalent of science nerds (and many are, and proudly so!) many are explorers and adventurers searching the material and spiritual realms for mystical knowledge. <br /> <br /> <b>The Fellowship of the One (the Fellowship) </b>- For many there is little difference between a religious experience and a magical one. For these mages magic is a gift from the Divine One. Starting as a group of mages in the Church of England this faction has grown to include any monotheist mage in Britain who is committed to using their magic for the moral and spiritual betterment of the country and its people. Jews, Catholics, Muslims, and even Hindus who hold a monotheist theology of Hindusim all belong although there is no question that the faction is still dominated by Anglicans and both in number and outlook. <br /> <br /> <b>Independents </b>- While most mages in Britain belong to one of the above factions there are some who chose to work on their own. And as Britain has become more multicultural small groups of mages (especially from South East Asia and more recently Eastern Europe) continue to maintain their specific cultural Magics and priorities. <br /> <br /> <b>A Note on Ethnic and Gender Diversity in British Magical Factions:</b> The membership of Britain\u2019s modern magical factions reflects the changing nature of Britain as a multicultural and egalitarian society. Since the 1950\u2019s Britain has become increasingly diverse, including immigrants from former colonies (e.g. India, Pakistan, Hong Kong, Jamaica), employees of corporations from all over the world, Europeans who have taken advantage of free movement in the European Union (especially a large influx from Poland in recent years), and most recently refugees from Africa and the Middle Esat. While they still have a long way to go, most of the major factions of British magic are ethnically, racially and gender inclusive. This is especially true of the Covenant, the City Sons (despite the un-PC name), the Fellowship, and the Collegium. While the Druids Circle and the Sovereigns are mostly gender diverse they are far less ethnically diverse than the other factions, not so much because of prejudice on the part of its members (although that certainly exists), but because their goals are far more tied to the history of Britain as it once was rather than how it is now. <br /> <br /> <b>Other Supernaturals and Magical Places</b><br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b> - Vampires are quite rare in the U.K. these days. As the population of Britain has increased so has the likelihood of mortals uncovering vampires and their feeding. While most vampires today are careful not to kill unless they have to, the modern world has made it far harder to hunt without being detected, especially in countries like Britain where the land mass is small and the population density is high. As a result, vampires in Britain are quite few and far between and they create networks or people and power around them, not in order to play Machiavellian political games, but to ensure their safety and continued survival. Most British vampires are perfectly happy with this reality as long as they remain well fed but some feel it is time to reestablish their former dominance over the human herd and remind them they are but cattle. <br /> <br /> <b>Changeling Breeds</b> - The majority of weres in Britain are werewolves, but wereravens, werecats and other two-natured also exist in the British Isles. Most of the changing breeds in Britain are either loners or organized in small packs or families patrolling their territories and taking care of their own. <br /> <br /> <b>Fae </b>- The Fair Folk have been a part of the British Isles since before recorded time. Changelings are a significant aspect of the British supernatural. In London the vast majority make their home in Underlondon. <br /> <br /> <b>Underlondon</b> - No one knows why or how but the building of the London Underground resulted in the creation of a spiritual pocket realm that grew with the tube system. While any supernatural is able to access Underlondon (through secret portals in tube stations functioning similarly to Platform 9 \u00be) the fae have found access easiest and the vast majority of Underlondon is populated by the fae. For the British changelings this concentration provides both a sense of community and safety in numbers from the threat of theTrue fae. Over time many of the areas of Underlondon have taken on aspects of the stations and overground areas they are connected with in the mundane realm so that Knightsbridge does in fact have a bridge and a Troll knight guarding the way, both Earl\u2019s Court and Queen\u2019s Park are courts of fae , and Piccadilly Circus is in fact home to a circus of weird, amazing and scary fae. <br /> <br /> <b>Grey Men</b> \u2013 Nobody knows who the Grey men really are, or if they do, they aren\u2019t telling. Grey Men activity has been reported since the middle ages in London but no one can discern their motives or purpose. Sometimes they help against the dark forces that threaten London and sometimes they seem to help them with little rhyme or reason. Some believe them to be an alien race (like the greys of UFO lore or from an otherworldly realm that encroaches on ours) while others argue they are servitors of a spirit or god of London, either one that lays dormant or serving as a \u201csecret service\u201d of sorts to a known power. Today Grey Men generally appear in grey business wear (with the occasional bowler hat and brolly for good measure) but are most memorable due to their utter lack of memorability. <br /> <br /> <b>Mundane Factions </b><br /> <br /> <b>The Institute</b> - Founded as the Institute for Metaphysical Studies by Sir Isaac Newton, the Institute represented the intersection between Newton\u2019s scientific work and his studies of the occult, at a time when the distinction between the two was still unclear to seekers of knowledge. Newton himself was only involved with the Institute for a brief time but it continued long after to study the supernatural by scientific means. Today the Institute is at a crossroads with many still committed to scientific study of the occult for its own sake, while others, including significant members of the inner sanctum, are making moves to monetize the occult and make a significant profit from selling the results of supernatural research to the highest bidder or an unsuspecting public. <br /> <br /> <b>The Watch</b> - During WWII neighborhood watches looked out for the neighborhoods ensuring their safety, rallying the community in times of need, and keeping an eye out for spies and criminals. And occasionally monsters. While people were distracted by the war effort some supernaturals got overly confident and hunted humans more openly than they might usually do. And they were noticed. Some among the neighborhood watches continued to be vigilant against the monsters after the war creating a loose network of hunters and protectors who defend their neighborhoods against the things that go bump in the night. <br /> <br /> <b>Network13.com</b> - Modern social media is full of crazy conspiracy theorists who believe the government is in cahoots with the Freemasons and the Illuminati to control the world. But once in a while they stumble across some actually truth. And even more rarely they uncover a truth about the supernatural. When they do they are contacted by Network 13 and connected with a small but growing network of people dedicated to uncovering the truths they believe the government is hiding about the supernatural. <br /> <br /> <b>The Dashwood Club</b> - Formerly known as the Hellfire Club, the Dashwood Club was formed in the mid-18th century as a gentleman\u2019s club dedicated to the pleasures of the flesh and to the revival of pagan fertility rituals. The club officially closed down in the 1780\u2019s but in reality it continued with a new purpose - the exploration of pleasure and power through magical means. Members seek new supernatural experiences to expand their consciousness and expand the boundaries of sensual pleasure through experimentation with the occult. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T02:50:48-07:00","id":1210874,"title":"","content":"I like this a lot and I should line to borrow some if I once more run a Mage game set in London or tgereabouts. In my game I incorporated the fact that London is possibly the most cosmopolitan city in the world as a game element: if you enter Shadow London you could find a &quot;Metropolis&quot; edifice, almost subway-like, that you could use to travel to any city in the world. A bit like city-walking in the Godmachine Chronicles. It was supposed to be a lot more costly and risky tha using Space magic though. Of course, the game never got going so the players never got there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T03:37:54-07:00","id":1210882,"title":"","content":"Nice. A few minor points on the Mages factions - the Orders <i>aren't</i> decendend from Atlantis (which, of course, never existed), but are creations of Mage society dating from after the time of Alexander. The Mysterium has extensive overlap with your Collegium, for example.<br /> <br /> For the mundane factions, have you read Hunter: the Vigil?<br /> <br /> Are the Grey Men God-Machine Angels, or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:20:16-07:00","id":1211022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1210882#post1210882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. A few minor points on the Mages factions - the Orders <i>aren't</i> decendend from Atlantis (which, of course, never existed), but are creations of Mage society dating from after the time of Alexander. The Mysterium has extensive overlap with your Collegium, for example.<br /> <br /> For the mundane factions, have you read Hunter: the Vigil?<br /> <br /> Are the Grey Men God-Machine Angels, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks. happy you like it! <br /> <br /> My understanding (which i will admit may have been flawed) was that Mages in NWoD/CofD did believe these groups could be be traced back to Atlantis. Whether that was true or not is a whole different issue and i just decided to side=step the question and avoid Atlantis altogether as anything other than a myth. <br /> <br /> Yes, the Collegium and the Mysterium are pretty similar and this was really the only NWoD Order that i mostly kept as it was but changed the name to sound more connected to an academic feel by referencing colleges at Universities like Oxford or Cambridge. <br /> <br /> I have read Hunter the Vigil and those are all great factions, some of which overlap with what i have here. <br /> <br /> I left the Grey men intentionally vague so they could be whatever they need to be. Honestly haven't decided what they truly are but no reason they can't be angels of the god machine if that's what you want!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:21:28-07:00","id":1211024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1210874#post1210874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this a lot and I should line to borrow some if I once more run a Mage game set in London or tgereabouts. In my game I incorporated the fact that London is possibly the most cosmopolitan city in the world as a game element: if you enter Shadow London you could find a &quot;Metropolis&quot; edifice, almost subway-like, that you could use to travel to any city in the world. A bit like city-walking in the Godmachine Chronicles. It was supposed to be a lot more costly and risky tha using Space magic though. Of course, the game never got going so the players never got there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it! I may use that in my game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:24:31-07:00","id":1211070,"title":"","content":"As it stands it's a little generic. You've got King Arthur and Druids, but otherwise it could basically be anywhere. There are a lot of opportunities for specific detail that aren't used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:19:40-07:00","id":1211120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211070#post1211070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands it's a little generic. You've got King Arthur and Druids, but otherwise it could basically be anywhere. There are a lot of opportunities for specific detail that aren't used.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe examples would help here. (I'm not a London native, so I am curious as well)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:43:29-07:00","id":1211136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211120#post1211120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe examples would help here. (I'm not a London native, so I am curious as well)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Examples of what precisely? What would help most in providing the appropriate colour and detail?<br /> <br /> To be clear by the way, this was just me sharing my setting as it currently exist and I have deliberately left lots vague so i can more easily fit in ideas and scenarios from wherever I get inspiration. But Could be good for my own thinking to think about what specific examples I already have and flesh them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:05:22-07:00","id":1211149,"title":"","content":"Not sure if its what people are looking for by way of examples (actually pretty sure it isn't) but here is some more stuff for more flavour.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Gods and Spirits of London</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>The Goddess Tamesis/Old Father Thames</b> - Tamesis was the Celtic goddess of fresh water and gave her name to the river Thames. Later the river\u2019s spiritual manifestation took on a male image as Old Father Thames. Once it was thought that these were two different spirits but most mages now recognize these are simply two sides to the same being, representing different aspects of the Thames - Tamesis representing the natural core of the river and Old Father Thames reflecting the people and trade that have come to rely on it. <br /> <br /> <b>Mother London</b> - Mother London is the spirit of the city. She has grown along with the city and her aspect has changed accordingly. Sometimes she presents herself as a proper English lady supping on tea and crumpets, sometimes as a Jamaican grandmother, or an Indian auntie, or a Jewish mother, or a passionate hipster, or a slick city professional. All and more are faces of Mother London in the modern age as the city grows and changes. <br /> <br /> <b>Herne/Cernunos</b> - The Celtic god Cernunos, later know as Herne by the Saxons, was the god of wild places. Much of London was once wild and parts still hold on to that nature. In those parts Herne still holds power and is worshiped by those who wish to keep the power of the wild strong even in the midst of the great city. <br /> <br /> <b>The Ripper King</b> - Jack the Ripper wasn\u2019t just one man on a murderous rampage. He was the manifestation of the dark spirit of the city, the Ripper King. Every city is a mix of good and bad, light an dark, growth and decay. The Ripper King is the spirit of all the dark, nasty, aspects of London, all the things people fear about city life and life in London in general. No one is sure whether the Ripper King is an ancient True Fae, a dark spirit or something else entirely but everyone is sure that the darkness of the city feeds him. And once in a while someone is possessed by that darkness and starts to kill. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:05:54-07:00","id":1211150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211136#post1211136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Examples of what precisely? What would help most in providing the appropriate colour and detail?<br /> <br /> To be clear by the way, this was just me sharing my setting as it currently exist and I have deliberately left lots vague so i can more easily fit in ideas and scenarios from wherever I get inspiration. But Could be good for my own thinking to think about what specific examples I already have and flesh them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comment was more directed at <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a>, since they said &quot;There are a lot of opportunities for specific detail that aren't used.&quot;, I was wondering what details they had in mind that were not being used. I haven't been to London, so I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:07:21-07:00","id":1211151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211150#post1211150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My comment was more directed at <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a>, since they said &quot;There are a lot of opportunities for specific detail that aren't used.&quot;, I was wondering what details they had in mind that were not being used. I haven't been to London, so I have no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm interested too! Hope to get clarification. Could be helpful for adding flavour to the setting for me too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:49:21-07:00","id":1211164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211120#post1211120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe examples would help here. (I'm not a London native, so I am curious as well)</div> </div> </div> </div>Two came to mind particularly.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the Circle. The growth of cities overtaking the countryside around it is really common all over the world. London though, has had a policy of creating green belts which aren't developed so you get a weird landscape of countryside within Greater London. It's been a contentious issue for decades and would fit right into the competition between the Circle and the Sons.<br /> <br /> With the Watch it's more that it seems to be referring to the Civil Defence Service and ARP Wardens but uses the more generic 'neighbourhood watch'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T16:28:58-07:00","id":1211209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211164#post1211164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two came to mind particularly.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the Circle. The growth of cities overtaking the countryside around it is really common all over the world. London though, has had a policy of creating green belts which aren't developed so you get a weird landscape of countryside within Greater London. It's been a contentious issue for decades and would fit right into the competition between the Circle and the Sons.<br /> <br /> With the Watch it's more that it seems to be referring to the Civil Defence Service and ARP Wardens but uses the more generic 'neighbourhood watch'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both good points. Also Hampstead Heath stands out as a place in London which maintains a certain aspect of the natural wild right next to residential and shopping areas that would absolutely be frequented by the more urbane members of the City Sons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T16:43:05-07:00","id":1211215,"title":"","content":"Also, as this is Mage-centric (I'm guessing based on which sub-forum it is in), what Mysteries are available and London specific? How is the Supernal reflected in London? What age-old Mysteries remain to be plumbed? Are you going to do anything with Myrddin/Merlin's Ascension?<br /> <hr /><br /> I'm guessing Werewolves and Fae have a bit more interaction with the Circle, (and more modern Werewolves with the Sons). Are you using Prometheans, Beasts, Mummies, or Demons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-24-2018, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:48:21-07:00","id":1211239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211215#post1211215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as this is Mage-centric (I'm guessing based on which sub-forum it is in), what Mysteries are available and London specific? How is the Supernal reflected in London? What age-old Mysteries remain to be plumbed? Are you going to do anything with Myrddin/Merlin's Ascension?<br /> <hr /><br /> I'm guessing Werewolves and Fae have a bit more interaction with the Circle, (and more modern Werewolves with the Sons). Are you using Prometheans, Beasts, Mummies, or Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>So have to be honest and say that my campaign has never focused on the Mage mythology or the meta plot from OWoD before that, so not much to say on those questions. <br /> <br /> As for the other supernatural groups, yes they are all there except the god machine demons. Really not a fan although I will admit that god machine angels make sense for the Grey Men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:02:07-07:00","id":1211244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211239#post1211239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So have to be honest and say that my campaign has never focused on the Mage mythology or the meta plot from OWoD before that, so not much to say on those questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much Mythology as Mechanics (at least, as of 2E). Mages are Addicted to the Mysteries - they need to investigate <i>something</i>. The Myrddin/Merlin Ascension isn't oWoD Metaplot (at least, as far as I know, since I don't follow Mage: the Ascension). I was referencing a Developer's commentary that Myrddin was a cunning Acanthus that exalted the symbols of Camelot, Ascended, and the pissed off Exarch did what they could to (unsuccessfully) scrub it from history/Time. It's semi-un-official, so it isn't required anyways. I just thought it was relevant and a nice nod to history and the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211239#post1211239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the other supernatural groups, yes they are all there except the god machine demons. Really not a fan although I will admit that god machine angels make sense for the Grey Men.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why the dislike for the Unchained? (Answer not needed - you feel how you feel, but if there are misconceptions, we might clear those up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:21:06-07:00","id":1211249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211244#post1211244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so much Mythology as Mechanics (at least, as of 2E). Mages are Addicted to the Mysteries - they need to investigate <i>something</i>. The Myrddin/Merlin Ascension isn't oWoD Metaplot (at least, as far as I know, since I don't follow Mage: the Ascension). I was referencing a Developer's commentary that Myrddin was a cunning Acanthus that exalted the symbols of Camelot, Ascended, and the pissed off Exarch did what they could to (unsuccessfully) scrub it from history/Time. It's semi-un-official, so it isn't required anyways. I just thought it was relevant and a nice nod to history and the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why the dislike for the Unchained? (Answer not needed - you feel how you feel, but if there are misconceptions, we might clear those up)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Myrdin/Merlin idea is interesting. Do you have a link to the source? I wonder if they are including that in the dark ages/Arthurian section of the dark eras 2. <br /> <br /> As for the god machine angels and demons it\u2019s reeally just a matter of personal taste. One of those things where I liked the idea but it just didn\u2019t work for me in practice. Happy to hear your views. Who knows. might change my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:32:54-07:00","id":1211255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211249#post1211249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Myrdin/Merlin idea is interesting. Do you have a link to the source?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vent's got the critical detail slightly off, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=952388#post952388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arthurian World did exist (in some form, it was probably closer to earlier Dark Ages, Arthur laughing as he wrestles bears and smites men versions than after it got lancelotted and romantic fantasied) sometime in post-Roman Britain. It was the pet project of a welsh Silver Ladder Acanthus (and either the founder of or an early member of the Walkers in Mists Legacy) with the Shadow Name of Myrddin (or, in English, Merlin). He achieved archmastery, and his Noumenon, the great act of magic that made him Ascend, was to manipulate Fate to great and then doom the society he built, marking the Symbolism of Arcadia forever. Among the side effects was turning the astral anthropomorphism of Fate into Mordred.<br /> <br /> Then the Arcadian Exarchs deleted the whole thing from the timeline, and history became as we know it. Myrddin, safely Ascended as the very symbol of a cunning bastard, gave no shits.<br /> <br /> <b>Tldr - it is a longstanding setting element of Mage, since Tome of the Watchtowers nearly ten years ago, that Merlin was a real mage, that the crystal cave was what he *wanted* (his ascension) and the fall of Camelot was entirely deliberate on his part.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T09:18:37-07:00","id":1211443,"title":"","content":"Well that's interesting! Any idea if this will be part of the Arthur's Britannia Dark Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:08:03-07:00","id":1211522,"title":"","content":"Don't know. Probably not - some people went and requested the gamelines for the Arthurian dark era and left Mage out. Dawkins knows the score, but its a little long for a one-line mention in a crossover sidebar.<br /> <br /> The Mage Arthurian thing will be in Tome of the Pentacle's history chapter, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:33:24-07:00","id":1211539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211522#post1211522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know. Probably not - some people went and requested the gamelines for the Arthurian dark era and left Mage out. Dawkins knows the score, but its a little long for a one-line mention in a crossover sidebar.<br /> <br /> The Mage Arthurian thing will be in Tome of the Pentacle's history chapter, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will you and the team be exploring the history of Mage society in other regions of the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T15:13:49-07:00","id":1211585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1208904-shadow-london-savage-urban-fantasy-in-the-uk?p=1211539#post1211539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will you and the team be exploring the history of Mage society in other regions of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s hard to imagine they wouldn\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}